<!--Post: 3497--><!--Time: 1104966415-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3497"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Affie4u<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Affie4u<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 3:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe BTK made that Phone call because he knew that he wasn&#39;t going to do anything eles for a few years so he figured, why not take a chance &amp; call &amp; report Nancy&#39;s murder. He must of knew then after he killed Nancy that he was going to go into hiding .<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3497-->
<!--Post: 3534--><!--Time: 1104982008-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3534"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 7:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That&#39;s possible but there have been other killers who have made phone calls after killing, and then continued to kill. One example would be that on 9/27/69 the Zodiac killer phoned after murdering one and severely injuring another. At the time, Zodiac though he had killed them both. His phone message -- he called the police -- was, &#34;I want to report a murder, no, a double murder. They are two miles north of Park Headquarters. They were in a white Karmen-Ghia.&#34; -- &#34;Where are you now?,&#34; Zodiac was asked, -- &#34;I&#39;m the one who did it.&#34; replied Zodiac, who then walked away from the phone. Fourteen days later, Zodiac murdered cab driver Paul Stine, in San Francisco. This is from the actual police report: <a href="http://www.zodiackiller.com/LBReport32.html" target=_top>http://www.zodiackiller.com/LBReport32.html</a>  <BR> <BR>There is a difference. BTK phoned from a short distance from the Fox crime scene. Zodiac&#39;s call was probably made twenty-seven miles from his crime scene. However, like BTK, Zodiac&#39;s call to the police was from a nearby pay phone. Also, BTK specifically mentioned Nancy Fox&#39;s name, Zodiac never named any names.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3534-->
<!--Post: 3632--><!--Time: 1105074969-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3632"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 9:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George,  <BR> <BR>It is worth pointing out that BTK in the Nancy Fox phone call &#40;like the Zodiac in this call&#41; went through the operator rather than dialing directly. Neither one of them seems to have had any apparent fear of apprehension as they had to know that the call would be traced to the phone they were on. I am willing to bet that neither phone yielded any fingerprints or other forensic evidence. &#40;Am I correct on that?&#41;  <BR> <BR>I am again struck by quality and quantity of the similarities of these two cases. Was BTK simply aping the Zodiac or IS HE the Zodiac. I am still not completely ready to dump that theory until I see some evidence to the contrary. The timelines could work and I have not yet seen one single piece of evidence that excludes BTK and the Zodiac being one and the same killer. It is important to remember that conjecture and calling people asking this question idiots, as some people tend to do &#40;this is NOT directed at you personally at all&#41; is not evidence excluding this possibility. If someone CAN exclude BTK and Zodiac being the same perpetrator through evidentiary means, I would REALLY love to see that evidence !<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3632-->
<!--Post: 3650--><!--Time: 1105083584-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3650"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 11:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Dpinva <BR> <BR>A third possibility is that Zodiac and BTK knew each other and had/have som kind of pact, maybe even more serial killers are members in that pact, a Serial Killers Lodge? <BR> <BR>skov<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3650-->
<!--Post: 3654--><!--Time: 1105085814-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3654"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 12:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The &#39;Serial Killers Lodge&#39; post is by far the most ridiculous post I have seen yet on this site. I hope you are kidding, if not you deserve at t-shirt or something. <BR>Sounds like a great title for a movie though.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3654-->
<!--Post: 3655--><!--Time: 1105086171-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3655"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 12:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Johno, I was tempted to post essentially what you just did. However, skov is convinced I have some kind of a grudge against her, so I decided against it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3655-->
<!--Post: 3656--><!--Time: 1105086368-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3656"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiquitah<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiquitah<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 12:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Skov: I think you are thinking way tooooo hard. <BR> <BR>Chill.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3656-->
<!--Post: 3661--><!--Time: 1105102555-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3661"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 4:55 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Skov, I respect your opinion on this one and all.....however, I think maybe we are starting to overreach just a touch here. I guess it is a remote possibility, ala Leopold and Loeb, that they might have known each other &#40;although the chances of this are, in my professional opinion, far less than both sets of crimes being one actor, which is also pretty unlikely but still completely unrefuted&#41;but chances of this would be in the 7 or 8 places to 1.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3661-->
<!--Post: 3680--><!--Time: 1105127117-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3680"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ryddik<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ryddik<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 11:45 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Has anyone ever saw the movie kiss the girls? Same idea 2 killers but on diffrent coasts same m.o. and in connection with one another good movie but not likely in dealing with serial killers. BTK just idolizes the idea of being &#34;uncatchable&#34; and feels a connectin with the zodiac in that aspect.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3680-->
<!--Post: 3701--><!--Time: 1105141399-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3701"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Shyra<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Shyra<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 3:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That&#39;s interesting info about the phone.  Thanks for providing that.  I know she never gave anyone her number.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3701-->
<!--Post: 3708--><!--Time: 1105147462-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3708"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 5:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><font color="#800000">Ryddick,</font> <BR> <BR><font color="#800000"><i>Kiss The Girls, </i>as well as the Sandra Bullock movie<i> Murder By Numbers, </i>are both loosely based on the Leopold and Loeb case. Leopold and Loeb were two spoiled rich kids who set out to commit a &#34;perfect&#34; murder in the 1930&#39;s and were caught despite, or perhaps because of, their arrogant game playing and competition with each other. </font> <BR> <BR><font color="#800000">Jean Desalve, a French multi-territorial serial killer who was also a historical case that served as additional background for <i>Kiss The Girls </i>&#40;and who is mentioned by the FBI agent in the scene where they find the &#34;lunar module&#34; in the California doctor&#39;s apartment in <i>Kiss The Girls</i>&#41;, confused the French police into <i>thinking </i>that he was actually two people because he not only murdered in two completely different territories but used two completely different MO&#39;s <i>and</i> signatures. I know very little about him other than what is in the movie, but it is interesting. As the FBI agent in <i>Kiss The Girls </i> states, Desalve was the rarest of serial killers - a true multi-territorial predator. In one locale he eviscerated his victims and in the other he &#40;I think&#41; strangled them &#40;or killed them by some more traditional means, if traditional is the correct word to use here&#41;. The point I am getting at here is that BTK and the Zodiac <i>might</i> have had a Leopold and Loeb thing going where they cooperated and competed &#40;with the Zodiac now long since dead or otherwise out of the picture&#41;, but it is somewhat more likely that either a Jean Delsave scenario in which BTK and the Zodiac are actually the same person with completely different signatures is the case, or, far and away the most likely scenario, that BTK admires the Zodiac and wants to impress and emulate him. BTK is probably a solo act, at least now - keeping his communications since last March secret and not getting caught would be exponentially more difficult with a partner. The earlier communications from the 1970&#39;s would have the same difficulties.  <BR> <BR>At the end of the day BTK is not organized or intelligent enough, although he is certainly both to some extent, to really successfully execute most of the conspiracy theories ascribed to him that seem to permeate many of the internet BTK boards. He is simply a psychopathic, sociopathic hate filled murderer that is plain and boring enough to not get noticed and therefore not get caught.  <BR> <BR>He is not stupid, but he is not a conspiratorial genius either. He is not playing out some intricately devised and executed grand plan - he is simply toying with everyone and, I believe, making it all up as he goes along, being driven by what ever obscene and demented demons it is that torment him and force him to torment and kill others. His next move is probably almost as big a surprise to him as it is to us.  <BR> <BR>For a real surprise, perhaps he will take up one of the people offering to listen to him directly to try to understand and help him &#40;like <i>themoodyblue </i>on C&amp;J and several people on Kansas.com&#41; and help him understand that his best chance for both help and lasting fame lies in turning himself in and truly being understood. Let&#39;s hope he is concerned enough  with his legacy to come forward and complete our understanding of his actions, motives and beliefs so that he will be enshrined in the annals of serial crime for a long, long time to come as one of the truly unique serial killers in history. There will <i>never </i>be another BTK.  <BR> <BR>Thank God.</font><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3708-->
